    "ratio": 8.43,
    "reading": "RAW ECE ranges 0.018 (shenzhen) to 0.153 (ostrava) \u2014 8.4x, and the pooled 0.109 describes no single site. BUT the disease-controlled panel shows most of that spread is CASE-MIX, not a site-specific calibration defect: holding the class constant collapses the range to 0.012-0.027 (2.3x) and every site is well calibrated on the class they share. Do not report the 8x. The defensible statements are (1) the model is over-confident where the cases are hard, by +0.109 pooled, and (2) a residual site effect survives the control at Ostrava (+0.027, CI excludes 0) but it is an order of magnitude smaller than the raw number suggests.",
    "controlled_ratio": 2.32,
    "methodological_point": "This is the third place in this paper where an uncontrolled aggregate overstated a site effect: the naive site probe (\u00a74.4), image-level AP-ROP recall (\u00a74.3), and now per-site ECE. Each time the control was available and cheap."
